{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 960,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm at the Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Pasadena,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4200,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm here to see the first drone that's gonna fly on another planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8800,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the Mars helicopter. Come on!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So this is our baby."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14840,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No way!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15800,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16880,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That thing right there is the actual machine that is going to take off and land on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22600,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's going with the Mars 2020 mission. That is the Mars helicopter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26560,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This will be the first powered flight in another planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30140,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How awesome is that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31720,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it's necessary to say first powered flight,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34600,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because in 1985, the Soviet Vega missions deployed two helium balloons on Venus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39920,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They transmitted data for over forty six hours while floating at an altitude of 54 kilometers in Venus's dense atmosphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which at the surface has a pressure of over 90 Earth atmospheres."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51320,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In contrast, Mars has very little atmosphere, only around 1% of Earth's."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56560,
    "dDurationMs": 8920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Flying this kind of helicopter is equivalent to flying a similar helicopter on Earth at a hundred thousand feet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65480,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you don't know, you don't hear about many helicopters at a hundred thousand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69160,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think forty thousand feet is probably the record."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I checked. Forty thousand feet is the record altitude reached by helicopters on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76320,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "85,000 feet is the highest a plane has ever flown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79720,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On Mars, the air is even thinner than that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right. In terms of density is 1% of what you have in this room."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this room, a cubic meter of air is about a kilogram."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah\n- The same cubic meter on Mars will be about 15 grams to 18 grams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95680,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So you have to push a lot of air down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes. You gotta get a lot of air flowing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the obvious trick, if you will, is to spin the blades faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105400,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It can spin between 2300 rpm and 2900 rpm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109320,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110240,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is fast. Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111800,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Here I'm trying to work out exactly how fast that is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I looked it up, and on Earth helicopters typically spin their rotors at around 500 rpm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121040,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the Mars helicopter will have to spin its blades five times faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125360,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But there are some limits you know, you really don't want to get the tips of the blades breaking the speed of sound,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131320,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- cause then you have shockwaves and all sorts of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133040,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- and you get all kinds of funky aerodynamics and you know the transonic flows and things like that, so you don't want to go there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we, in our designs, keep the tip Mach numbers down to below about 0.7."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143560,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So 70% the speed sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145040,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah. It was very conservative."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146360,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- One advantage of flying on Mars is that gravity is only 38% of what it is on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152080,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even so, making the craft lightweight was essential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155320,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Keeping the mass of this vehicle contained during the entire design process has been the major challenge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160560,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Every single part had to be considered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164000,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The entire vehicle is less than 1.8 kilograms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166840,
    "dDurationMs": 520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Woah!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167360,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So, less than four pounds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168560,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's about the same as this laptop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171120,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The blades are a foam core with carbon fiber layup. Each of them is about 35 grams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177640,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Wow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178040,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes, it's quite light. Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181120,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- 35 grams is the mass of six quarters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184400,
    "dDurationMs": 10880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think about that: two 35 gram blades lifting an 1800 gram helicopter by spinning 40 times per second in just 1% of Earth's atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195280,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How long can it fly for?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It's designed to fly up to 90 seconds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200560,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- A minute and a half of flight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202000,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202480,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- To me that sounds like forever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204560,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you're talking about another planet, flying autonomously by itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 1/100 earth atmosphere, I mean, come on!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210840,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, that's a long time!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212440,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is. Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213120,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- One of the questions I had was, why didn't they use a quadcopter design?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, because on Mars, the blades have to be so long that the whole craft would barely fit on the rover."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223600,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two counter-rotating propellers provide the simplest design."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also generate lift more efficiently when stacked on top of each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232200,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The bottom rotor sees the sort of the more compactified flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238280,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The top one pulls it, the bottom one sees sort of a more concentrated flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242800,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the bottom rotor actually can do better than if they were separated apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But how do you test a helicopter designed for conditions on Mars on Earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250760,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What would happen if you just took your Mars helicopter and you tried to take off on Earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256560,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It would just make a lot of noise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257960,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Really?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And it probably wouldn't get the full head speed either..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260440,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- because of how much atmosphere we've got."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262240,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Exactly, it's like trying to swim in a thick soup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263920,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a really amazing chamber here on lab called the 25-foot space simulator."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268040,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in that chamber you could simulate any kind of atmosphere you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271520,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can go to Martian pressures, you can stay at Earth pressures, whatever you want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274360,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that only took care of half of the problem, that was the aerodynamics aspect of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278240,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's the other part which is the gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280200,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We needed a way to fake Mars' gravity here on Earth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283600,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the best way that we could figure out to do that was a gravity offload."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286760,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Gravity offload just means pulling up on the helicopter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it only has to support about 38% of its weight just like it will have to do on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295080,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And effectively it was a high-tech fishing reel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297200,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so taking a brushed DC motor, a reaction torque sensor, and a pulley,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301080,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mounting that a couple stories in the air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then attaching a fishing string to the top of the helicopter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306360,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would tug the necessary force required to offload the differences in gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310880,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- An actual fishing line?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312120,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah, real fishing line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313200,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But isn't that stretchy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314600,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like don't you want something that's perfectly rigid so as soon as you apply the torque it gets applied to the craft?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318880,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right right, and we did a lot of testing with different vendors to find out which fishing line had the best spring constant for us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324680,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What does the helicopter sound like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I imagined that in 1% of Earth's atmosphere, the helicopter would be pretty quiet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332040,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah you're still at 1%, but it's still, real loud."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335200,
    "dDurationMs": 560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Really?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335760,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah we have audio recordings of it too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337520,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's it's, I would characterize it more like a 'baaaaaaaaah', something like that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343120,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(baaaaaaah)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346560,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When gravity offload systems working and the chamber was pumped down, the helicopter thought it was on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351640,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It felt like it was on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353960,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How do you actually steer this thing around and drive it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So the way helicopters work is they have something called collective and cyclic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what collectives do is they change the pitch on the blades uniformly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366960,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So throughout the entire revolution you will move the collective,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the blades will change, you can change your angle of attack, you'll get more lift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that's basically what you would provides you height control,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right? You pitch more you go up, pitch less you come down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then, there's something called a cyclic on helicopters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383320,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which basically what it does is it modulates the pitch as it goes around,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389040,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it can pitch it a little bit more here, less here, so it kind of like modulates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394200,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what that does is it provides an asymmetric torque, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you're pitched up there you get that additional torque."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400040,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you get it, depending upon the stiffness the system you actually get it with that a gyroscopic lag that can happen afterwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406960,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So once you get an asymmetric torque, the vehicle wants to start pitching or rolling. Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414200,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So once it pitches and rolls,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416600,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're doing it stably."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418400,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are now pointed in a direction and your thrust vector now has a component that's horizontal in the direction that you pitched. Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425480,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So then you start translating in that direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I've heard that initially someone tried to fly it with a joystick?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432240,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes.\n- Was it an early prototype?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- If you were sitting right there on Mars and you were trying to joystick it, what is it like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's almost unflyable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439040,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the reason for that it's the aerodynamics of when you want to command a roll to the left"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444760,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you see yourself starting to move to the right and you start commanding a roll to the left."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448640,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a delay aspect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450160,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that that delay effect makes it very very difficult for a human to try and pilot it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You can't fly this from Earth..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- because of the twenty-minute kind of time delay, so you have to really send sequences."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462760,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So essentially you're gonna push a button,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and like 20 minutes later it'll take off and do its thing and then you will find out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469280,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The way this flies autonomously,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471200,
    "dDurationMs": 9360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it has onboard gyros, onboard accelerometers and onboard camera,  an altimeter and an inclinometer;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so using that sensor suite,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482640,
    "dDurationMs": 8040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real-time measurement, you know against terrain and of course the gyros and the accelerometers sensing onboard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490680,
    "dDurationMs": 8520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the real-time estimation of the state of the vehicle is made continuously again at hundreds of Hertz"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499200,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then that's fed into the closed-loop control algorithm,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503400,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that takes the estimated state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then generates the correction that's needed at the blade level,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510720,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then the blades are continuously being controlled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513000,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you see video tapes of our \"successful flights\", right!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518400,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the vehicle looks dead calm, it's coming up, and hovering, and going laterally, coming back;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525280,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know the machines are working very very fast and very very hard it just looks very calm, but yes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531240,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the the blades are being continuously controlled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That is amazing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535280,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How will it handle a gentle breeze?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537880,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- A lot of the movies depict\n- Dust storms?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541020,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- The big dust storms as being very aggressive on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543840,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The truth of the matter is that with 1% Earth's atmosphere, there is very little matter actually hitting you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550000,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I mean, you're using that to lift yourself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552240,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Exactly, so there's enough to lift, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we also need to spend at 2200 rpms to be in the ballpark of lifting ourselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558840,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We built our own wind tunnel that we put inside this 25 foot chamber."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562080,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How many fans was it, Teddy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563760,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "960 computer fans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565800,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, but it does sound like a like a jet engine taking off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568720,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we built a fan wall array, it's called an open cross-section wind tunnel, where you don't need the walls,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just the fact of having an array of fans we are very confident of being able to go at 11 meters per second,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579960,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this vehicle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581200,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if I had known that somewhere along the way I'd be building a wind tunnel to do this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585400,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would have probably not taken the job on, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588160,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- How long does it take to recharge?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589840,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We recharge the whole day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591640,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the whole day at Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593720,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right. But does that mean that you could do one flight a day kind of thing? In theory?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597920,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In theory, yes, by design it can."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600160,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What is the size of the battery?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Between 35 and 40 watt hours total."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 605320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's equivalent to just three smartphone batteries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609080,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And get this -- most of that energy isn't even used for flying."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613280,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It has to survive temperatures as low as about minus 80 to minus hundred degrees C at night."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618520,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we keep the batteries warm and we surround the batteries with our electronics board so the electronic boards also stay warm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625000,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We take approximately two-thirds of energy just keeping things warm and warming things up to operate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only one-third of the energy is available for flight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632480,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Do you have insulation on there to keep it warm?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635160,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes. When you look at that helicopter, right, you have the solar panel on top with antenna,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640480,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then next is the rotor system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then bottom what you see this cube, is what we call the fuselage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646000,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are seeing it now actually uncovered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648440,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you're seeing the last day of final. We're recovering for delivery to be integrated onto the rover."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654400,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "okay so usually you won't be seeing that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656560,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the center of the cube is the ring of batteries, okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is space between the battery and the circuit boards that you are seeing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664920,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then there will be a shell that we put on called the fuselage shell,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669520,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that will close like CO2, the gas, around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674760,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the enclosure itself we're using the CO2 gas as the insulation material"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680240,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh wow! No aerogel?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682240,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- No aerogel. We did it consider it. It was in the game,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685720,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was in the consideration in the beginning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688640,
    "dDurationMs": 9320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it turns out that just the CO2 as insulator itself was sufficient for us to close our thermal model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697960,
    "dDurationMs": 360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698320,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And so guess why we wouldn't want to use aerogel if we have a choice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702320,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Weight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703080,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yep, there you go. Welcome to our team"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Now before the helicopter can experience the frigid conditions on Mars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709240,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first it has to get there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711040,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's a reminder that not only is this an aircraft, it's also a spacecraft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715880,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It has to survive launch."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717380,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has to survive launch loads which, you know, easily exceed about 80G"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722840,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, because of the vibration. Vibrational loads are 80G."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725760,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah.\nThen it has to survive the seven-month trip, complete with radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730440,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally after pulling nine Gs on entry into the Martian atmosphere the helicopter needs to be deployed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is gonna be on the rover, before you take off, does the rover like pick you up and put you down somewhere?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742680,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We're gonna be stowed underneath the rover on the belly pan on our side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746800,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there's gonna be several several sequences of firings of explosive devices"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752560,
    "dDurationMs": 3259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to actually rotate us right side up and then drop us on the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755819,
    "dDurationMs": 5101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- For example the very last thing the rover does is it's got us by this bolt, it's holding us about this high,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760920,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then it goes has to drop us, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762720,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So how do you undo a bolt on, on a spacecraft?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766000,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You blow it up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766600,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You blow it up. Basically it's materials you know undergoes a phase transition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771120,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which suddenly increases the, the stress in the metal part of the thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and makes the bolt break. It's called a frangibolt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778840,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Then once we're on the surface, the rover drives over us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it gets about 100 meters away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783160,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then we have about a two-hour counter internally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787120,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where we'll wake up after 2 hours, wait to hear some RF transmissions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791080,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if we do get that link with the rover then great."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793920,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Our base station on the rover would issue the fly now command."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797720,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First flight will probably be a mutual selfie, you would think.."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801040,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is after all the selfie age."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804640,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I like that as the goal of the first flight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes it is. In fact, it is good to know the best time to fly this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is at 11 o'clock in the morning local time on Mars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that the reason for that is, we would have come out of the night,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where we would have spent a lot of battery power trying to you know stay warm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820240,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 11 o'clock, the state of the charge would have gotten to the point where you could fly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824920,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without risking a brownout on the battery and then, you know, dropping the whole craft to the ground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829600,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also 11 o'clock is where the Sun would have warmed up things,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833880,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we don't quite have to heat up as much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And also it's not late afternoon where because of the warmth, the density has begun to drop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "okay, and the winds have begun to pick up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844640,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, what we will investigate is after we get the first couple of flights under our belt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849640,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm sure we will try to fly in the afternoon and you know do more exploratory things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853920,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the most conservative thing we can do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856240,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to sort of pick a mid-morning flight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858840,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So what is the purpose of this mission?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861440,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Mars helicopter is first and foremost a technology demonstration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865520,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to prove that we can fly on another planet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869200,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The helicopter can take color photos and videos, but its purpose is not to make scientific discoveries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead it is to help engineers figure out how to design and build aircraft for future missions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881200,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You can imagine something that's about 30 kilograms carrying you know a 2 kilogram science payload, doing exploration,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "acting like a scout, like a small vehicle, like this, scouting ahead for some future rover;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893200,
    "dDurationMs": 8640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or it could be a gadget that goes and picks up some kind of samples and brings it back to a central lander for more sophisticated analysis;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or it could be a completely standalone craft, and maybe more than one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905120,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are exploring places where humans and rovers can't get to easily:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911360,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "polar ice caps, you know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913560,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sides of cliffs and so forth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915440,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the real emphasis here is to try to get back all the engineering data so that it can inform that future design."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Flying on other planets will provide a new dimension in space exploration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An aircraft is faster and capable of covering more ground than a rover"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it can provide higher resolution imagery than an orbiting spacecraft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935240,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So maybe one day, aircrafts will be the companions of future rovers or even astronauts exploring other worlds."
    } ]
  } ]
}
